  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Gender Transformative and Youth Inclusive Democracy in Malawi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In achieving the specific objective of the Action of &#x2018;Enhanced inclusion of women, youth and marginalized groups to meaningfully participate in political and decision -making structures and processes&apos;, the proposed project will work at multiple levels; macro level (national and policy level) meso level (district councils), and micro level (women, youth, marginalised groups and community members in the targeted areas) to achieve the change. The project  will use the Oxfam&apos;s Model on Transformative Women&apos;s Leadership and Rights which has five pillars and addresses intersectionality (i) Building consciousness and capabilities of women, youth and marginalised at individual and collective levels (ii) Support to sustainability of Women&apos;s agencies through influencing resources (iii) Working on tackling norms and exclusionary practices affecting the targeted groups (iv) influencing rules and practices in politics and ( v) promoting social accountability initiatives on women youth and marginalised groups participation in political processes and decision making. The work will engage informal and formal domains and seek change at individual and systemic levels. The Action will see this change through the increased number of women, youth and marginalised groups who will be holding positions as Members of Parliament, Councillors and in leadership positions in development committees and through sustained women&apos;s rights organisations and civil society engagement on Malawi&apos;s inclusive political processes.</narrative>
  </description>
